examples.question_text:
In the parallelogram, side $a$ is chosen as the base.
(a) Identify its matching perpendicular height.
(b) Can the same height be used with side $c$? Explain why side $s$ is not its height.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (5,0);\coordinate (C) at (6.5,3);\coordinate (D) at (1.5,3);\coordinate (H) at (1.5,0);
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,below] {$a$};\draw (B)--(C) node[midway,right] {$s$};\draw (C)--(D) node[midway,above] {$c$};\draw (D)--(A);\draw[dashed] (D)--(H) node[midway,right] {$h$};
\coordinate (ra) at ($(H)!0.3cm!(D)$);\coordinate (rb) at ($(H)!0.3cm!(B)$);\draw (ra)--($(ra)+(rb)-(H)$)--(rb);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Side $PQ$ is chosen as the base of this triangle. Which labelled segment is its perpendicular height?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (P) at (0,0);\coordinate (Q) at (3.5,0);\coordinate (R) at (5,2.6);\coordinate (H) at (5,0);
\draw (P)--(Q) node[midway,below] {$PQ$};\draw (Q)--(R) node[midway,right] {$s$};\draw (R)--(P);\draw[dashed] (Q)--(H);\draw[dashed] (R)--(H) node[midway,right] {$t$};
\coordinate (ra) at ($(H)!0.3cm!(R)$);\coordinate (rb) at ($(H)!0.3cm!(Q)$);\draw (ra)--($(ra)+(rb)-(H)$)--(rb);\node[above] at (R) {$R$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

(a) Choose $p$ as the base. Identify its height.
(b) Choose $q$ as the base. Identify its height.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);\coordinate (A) at (4,0);\coordinate (B) at (0,3);
\draw (O)--(A) node[midway,below] {$p$};\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,above right] {$r$};\draw (B)--(O) node[midway,left] {$q$};
\coordinate (ra) at ($(O)!0.3cm!(A)$);\coordinate (rb) at ($(O)!0.3cm!(B)$);\draw (ra)--($(ra)+(rb)-(O)$)--(rb);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The vertical side is chosen as the base of this parallelogram. Which labelled segment is its perpendicular height?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (0,3);\coordinate (C) at (4,4);\coordinate (D) at (4,1);\coordinate (H) at (0,1);
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,left] {base};\draw (B)--(C);\draw (C)--(D) node[midway,right] {$v$};\draw (D)--(A) node[midway,below right] {$w$};\draw[dashed] (H)--(D) node[midway,above] {$u$};
\coordinate (ra) at ($(H)!0.3cm!(B)$);\coordinate (rb) at ($(H)!0.3cm!(D)$);\draw (ra)--($(ra)+(rb)-(H)$)--(rb);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The sloping side labelled $b$ is chosen as the base. Identify its matching height.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (4,2);\coordinate (C) at (1,4);\coordinate (H) at ($(A)!(C)!(B)$);
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,below right] {$b$};\draw (B)--(C) node[midway,above right] {$s$};\draw (C)--(A);\draw[dashed] (C)--(H) node[midway,left] {$k$};
\coordinate (ra) at ($(H)!0.3cm!(C)$);\coordinate (rb) at ($(H)!0.3cm!(B)$);\draw (ra)--($(ra)+(rb)-(H)$)--(rb);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The bottom side $AB$ is chosen as the base of this parallelogram. Show a matching perpendicular height.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (4.8,0);\coordinate (C) at (6.2,2.6);\coordinate (D) at (1.4,2.6);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--(D)--cycle;
\path (A)--(B) node[midway,below] {$AB$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Draw a segment from the opposite side to base $AB$, meeting the base at $90^{\circ}$. One matching height is shown.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (4.8,0);\coordinate (C) at (6.2,2.6);\coordinate (D) at (1.4,2.6);\coordinate (H) at (1.4,0);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--(D)--cycle;
\path (A)--(B) node[midway,below] {base $AB$};
\draw[dashed] (D)--(H);
\path (D)--(H) node[midway,right] {height};
\draw (1.4,0.25)--(1.65,0.25)--(1.65,0);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.question_text:
The top side is chosen as the base of this parallelogram. Which labelled segment is its matching perpendicular height?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,3.4);\coordinate (B) at (3.8,3.4);\coordinate (C) at (6,0);\coordinate (D) at (2.2,0);\coordinate (H) at (0,0);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--(D)--cycle;
\path (A)--(B) node[midway,above] {base};
\path (B)--(C) node[midway,right] {$r$};
\draw[dashed] (D)--(H)--(A);
\path (H)--(A) node[midway,left] {$t$};
\draw (0,3.15)--(0.25,3.15)--(0.25,3.4);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Segment $t$ meets the chosen base at $90^{\circ}$ and reaches the extended line of the opposite side. It is the matching height, even though it lies outside the parallelogram.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,3.4);\coordinate (B) at (3.8,3.4);\coordinate (C) at (6,0);\coordinate (D) at (2.2,0);\coordinate (H) at (0,0);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--(D)--cycle;
\path (A)--(B) node[midway,above] {base};
\path (B)--(C) node[midway,right] {$r$};
\draw[dashed] (D)--(H)--(A);
\path (H)--(A) node[midway,left] {$t$ (height)};
\draw (0,3.15)--(0.25,3.15)--(0.25,3.4);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.question_text:
Side $AB$ is chosen as the base of this triangle. Show its matching perpendicular height.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (2.4,2.4);\coordinate (C) at (4.8,1.2);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\path (A)--(B) node[midway,above left] {$AB$};
\path (A) node[below left] {$A$};\path (B) node[above left] {$B$};\path (C) node[right] {$C$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Extend base $AB$ beyond $B$. Draw a segment from the opposite vertex $C$ to the extended base, meeting it at $90^{\circ}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (2.4,2.4);\coordinate (C) at (4.8,1.2);\coordinate (H) at (3,3);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\path (A)--(B) node[midway,above left] {$AB$};
\draw[dashed] (B)--(H);\draw[dashed] (C)--(H);
\path (C)--(H) node[midway,above right] {height};
\draw (3.1768,2.8232)--(3,2.6464)--(2.8232,2.8232);
\path (A) node[below left] {$A$};\path (B) node[above left] {$B$};\path (C) node[right] {$C$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
